msgid "|morpheus| API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:18
msgid "Initial Considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:20
msgid ""
"Since we're creating Groups in a second Tenant, you'll need to have at "
"least one other Tenant in your appliance (|AdmTen|). You'll also need "
"access to a user account within the Subtenant which has rights to create "
"Groups. You could use a pre-existing user account or create a service "
"user for automated processes like this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:22
msgid ""
"Impersonate or log in with your service account and create an API Key. "
"API Keys are created by clicking on the user's name in the upper-right "
"corner of the application window, then clicking User Settings. On the "
"User Settings page, click :guilabel:`API ACCESS`. Next to one of the "
"entries (it doesn't matter which one but be careful about overwriting a "
"key that is already in use), click ACTIONS and then Generate. Copy the "
"Access Token into a secure place you can retrieve it from in the next "
"step. You will not be able to see this key again after closing the modal "
"containing the API Keys. Return to your primary |morpheus| account in the"
" original Tenant to continue with the guide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:25
msgid "Create Cypher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:27
msgid ""
"Cypher is a secure key/value store in |morpheus|. Using Cypher, we can "
"securely store passwords and other secret values (such as API keys) which"
" can then be called into automation Tasks and templates. Here we will "
"store the API Key for our service account user so we can call it into "
"automation scripts in a later step. In the |morpheus| UI, go to |TooCyp| "
"and click :guilabel:`+ ADD`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:29
msgid ""
"There are a number of different types of Cypher keys, which are useful in"
" different contexts. Here we'll use the \"secret\" type which allows us "
"to enter some known value which can be securely accessed later. Enter the"
" following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:31
msgid "**KEY:** secret/subusertoken"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:32
msgid "**VALUE:** Enter |morpheus| API Key for the Subtenant user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:33
msgid "**LEASE:** 0 (Lease time is given in seconds, with \"0\" being unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:35
msgid "Click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:37
msgid ".. image:: /images/opworkguide/createcypher.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:40
msgid "Create Inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:42
msgid ""
"Inputs are custom input fields which can be added to Layouts, Instance "
"Types, Workflows, and other constructs in |morpheus|. The input can be "
"consumed as variables within templates and scripts. In this case, the "
"Inputs will be associated with our Operational Workflow. We will create "
"three so the user can define a name for the new Group and optionally "
"provide a code and/or location value if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:44
msgid ""
"In |morpheus| UI, navigate to |LibOptInp|. Click :guilabel:`+ ADD`. "
"Complete the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:46
msgid ""
"**NAME:** Subtenant Group Name (The friendly name for the Input object in"
" |morpheus|)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:47
msgid ""
"**FIELD NAME:** subgroupname (The internal property which the input value"
" is assigned to)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:48
msgid ""
"**TYPE:** Text (The input type, in this case an open text field for the "
"user)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:49
msgid ""
"**LABEL:** Subtenant Group Name (The label the user sees next to the "
"input field)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:50
msgid ""
"**REQUIRED:** Checked (A name value is required for our Group so this "
"Input should be marked required. The other two Inputs we'll create will "
"not be required as they are optional fields when creating a Group)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:52
#: ../../getting_started/guides/op_workflows.rst:92
msgid "Once done, click :guilabel:`SAVE CHANGES`."
msgstr ""

